1
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:09,336
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode one. Our Planet!

2
00:00:18,039 --> 00:00:21,764
One sunny morning, Luna was spinning her old globe.

3
00:00:21,964 --> 00:00:25,614
Luna, why do you keep spinning that ball? Can I nap on it?

4
00:00:25,814 --> 00:00:29,476
It's a globe, Whiskers! A little model of our whole world, the Earth.

5
00:00:29,676 --> 00:00:31,751
So the Earth is round? Like a ball?

6
00:00:31,951 --> 00:00:35,052
Yes! The Earth is a giant ball, floating in space.

7
00:00:38,522 --> 00:00:41,677
But the garden is flat. I've napped on all of it.

8
00:00:41,877 --> 00:00:45,648
That's because the Earth is so big, it looks flat when you're standing on it.

9
00:00:53,043 --> 00:00:55,773
Want to see the whole world? Hold on to the cushion!

10
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:11,123
Whoosh! Up, up into space they flew!

11
00:01:11,323 --> 00:01:13,195
Wow! The Earth really is a ball!

12
00:01:13,395 --> 00:01:18,112
Now watch. A map is the globe, flattened out, so we see the whole world at once.

13
00:01:26,815 --> 00:01:28,708
Look, here's our home. You are here!

14
00:01:31,524 --> 00:01:33,931
Every map has four directions.

15
00:01:36,748 --> 00:01:39,905
North is up at the top. South is down at the bottom.

16
00:01:40,105 --> 00:01:42,507
East is this way, and west is that way.

17
00:01:42,707 --> 00:01:46,119
Never Eat Soggy Waffles! North, east, south, west!

18
00:01:46,319 --> 00:01:50,146
I would never eat soggy waffles. Crispy ones, though...

19
00:01:53,290 --> 00:01:55,714
Hey, why is there so much blue everywhere?

20
00:01:55,914 --> 00:01:58,286
Blue means water. Let's go and find out!

21
00:02:14,184 --> 00:02:17,388
They landed far out in the big blue ocean.

22
00:02:22,821 --> 00:02:26,721
Well, hello there, little travellers! Welcome to my ocean.

23
00:02:26,921 --> 00:02:28,600
Aaah! A talking rock!

24
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:33,233
I'm not a rock! I'm Grandpa Shelby, the oldest turtle in the sea.

25
00:02:33,433 --> 00:02:38,851
I swam all the way around the world. I kept going the same way, and came back home!

26
00:02:39,051 --> 00:02:40,547
Because the Earth is round!

27
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:52,017
Grandpa Shelby, is there really that much water?

28
00:02:52,217 --> 00:02:57,637
Oh, yes. If you cut the Earth into four parts, almost three of them would be water.

29
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:08,272
Only one part is land.

30
00:03:08,472 --> 00:03:11,009
So the world is mostly... fish soup?

31
00:03:13,826 --> 00:03:17,132
Ho ho! Climb on! Let's swim around the world!

32
00:03:28,451 --> 00:03:33,874
So they swam east, past Africa and Australia, across the giant Pacific.

33
00:03:38,653 --> 00:03:41,958
Stop! The edge of the map! We'll fall off the world!

34
00:03:51,969 --> 00:03:54,169
Whiskers, you can open your eyes now.

35
00:03:54,369 --> 00:03:55,745
Am I in space?

36
00:03:55,945 --> 00:03:59,744
No! We came out on the other side. The two edges of the map join up!

37
00:04:13,026 --> 00:04:17,741
A round Earth has no edge. Keep going, and you come back to the start.

38
00:04:17,941 --> 00:04:21,935
I knew that. I screamed on purpose. It was a sailor song.

39
00:04:28,676 --> 00:04:32,135
Remember! One. The Earth is round, like a ball.

40
00:04:35,279 --> 00:04:38,688
Two. Almost three quarters of the Earth is water.

41
00:04:41,831 --> 00:04:46,500
Three. Maps show four directions. North, south, east and west.

42
00:04:53,895 --> 00:04:58,679
Quiz time! Is the Earth flat like a pancake, or round like a ball?

43
00:05:02,150 --> 00:05:04,444
Round like a ball! Well done!

44
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:10,943
Next. Is there more land, or more water on Earth?

45
00:05:14,413 --> 00:05:18,370
More water! Almost three quarters of the Earth is water.

46
00:05:27,073 --> 00:05:29,788
And with a twinkle, they were home again.

47
00:05:29,988 --> 00:05:32,254
Let's swim around the world again tomorrow!

48
00:05:32,454 --> 00:05:36,205
Sure. But first, a nap. All the way around this cushion.

49
00:05:40,984 --> 00:05:44,989
Next time, the seven continents! Goodnight, round world.

